    <statement><p>If <m>z = \left(x+y\right)e^{y}</m> and <m>x = u^{2}+v^{2}</m> and <m>y = u^{2}-v^{2}</m>, 
find the following partial derivatives using
the chain rule.  Enter your answers as
functions of <m>u</m> and <m>v</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial z}{\partial u} =</m> 
<fillin characters="80" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial z}{\partial v} =</m>
<fillin characters="80" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4ue^{u^{2}-v^{2}}+2u^{2}e^{u^{2}-v^{2}}\cdot 2u</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2u^{2}e^{u^{2}-v^{2}}\cdot 2v</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
